            <ArticleTitle>Surgical Treatment of Snapping Scapula Syndrome Due to Malunion of Rib Fractures.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>e143-e144</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="pii" ValidYN="Y">S0003-4975(16)30964-X</ELocationID>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1016/j.athoracsur.2016.07.061</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>This report describes a case of snapping scapula syndrome (SSS) caused by malunited rib fractures. Abrasion of the deformed ribs was performed with good results. SSS as a cause of shoulder pain after thoracic trauma has to be considered and can be treated by a surgical abrasion technique.</AbstractText>
